Article 47

Involvement of various companies, labor unions, non-governmental organizations, and the Community in the elimination of economic and/or sexual exploitation of Children as referred to in Article 44 letter c shall be carried out through:
a. formulation of policies on the elimination of economic and/or sexual exploitation of Children in their environment;
b. cooperation to prevent Children from being exploited economically and/or sexually;
c. campaigns for the elimination of economic and/or sexual exploitation of Children;
d. increased supervision to prevent Children from being exploited economically and/or sexually;
e. company support for the elimination of exploitation of Children through corporate social responsibility; andf. reporting to the competent authorities if there is economic and/or sexual exploitation of Children.

Article 48

In the event that Children Who Are Exploited Economically and/or Sexually require restoration of their condition to its original state, services must be provided in the form of:
a. medical rehabilitation;
b. Social rehabilitation;
c. legal assistance and social assistance; and/or d. repatriation and Social Reintegration.

Article 76

1. Special Protection for Child Victims of Physical and/or Psychological Violence as referred to in Article 32 paragraph (1) letter i shall be carried out through efforts to:a. disseminate and socialize the provisions of laws and regulations that protect child victims of violence; andb. monitor, report, and impose sanctions.
