Article 93

Special Protection for Children Victims of Terrorism Networks shall also be provided in the form of:
a. fulfillment of the rights of Children Victims of Terrorism Networks to care and psychological health recovery;
b. medical rehabilitation;
c. reeducation and Social Reintegration;andd. safety guarantees both physical, mental, and social for Children Victims of Terrorism Networks.

Article 59

Physical and mental health recovery as referred to in Article 55 paragraph (1) shall be provided in the form of:
a. psychosocial therapy;
b. counseling;
c. beneficial activities;
d. referral to hospitals, safe houses, service centers, or other alternative places according to needs; and/ore. resocialization.

Article 83

1. Social Rehabilitation as referred to in Article 81 letter b shall be carried out in the form of:a. motivation and psychosocial diagnosis;
b. care and nurturing;
c. vocational training and entrepreneurship development; d. mental spiritual guidance;
e. physical guidance;
f. social guidance and psychosocial Counseling;
g. accessibility services;
h. social assistance and aid;
i. resocialization guidance;
j. follow-up guidance; and/orek. referral.
2. In addition to the forms as referred to in paragraph (1), Social Rehabilitation shall be carried out in the form of:a. physical therapy;
b. mental spiritual therapy;
c. psychosocial therapy;
d. therapy for livelihood;
39-
e. fulfillment of decent living;
f. accessibility support; and/orag. other forms that support social functioning.

Article 35

1. Special Protection as referred to in Article 34 paragraph (1) shall be carried out through:a. prevention so that Children do not become victims in emergency situations;
b. recording the number of Children requiring Special Protection in emergency situations;
c. mapping the basic and specific needs of Children requiring Special Protection in emergency situations;
d. guarantee of security and safety of Children in Emergency Situations;
e. recording of Children and their families for tracing and family reunification;
f. priority emergency rescue, evacuation, and security measures;
g. restoration of physical and psychological health;
h. provision of legal assistance, accompaniment, physical, psychological, and social rehabilitation of Children in Emergency Situations;
i. care;
j. improvement of facilities needed by Children in Emergency Situations;
k. fulfillment of basic and special needs of Children consisting of food, clothing, housing, education, provision of health services, learning and recreation, security guarantees, and equal treatment;
22-
l. fulfillment of special needs for Children with Disabilities and Children experiencing psychosocial problems;
m. exemption from education fees whether conducted in formal or non-formal Educational Institutions during the emergency period; andn. provision of services for the fulfillment of Children's identity rights and important documents lost due to emergency situations; and/orProvision of Social Reintegration services.
2. Special Protection for Children in Emergency Situations as referred to in paragraph (1) must be received by Children in Emergency Situations as soon as possible, the implementation of which shall be in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.
3. Provision of services for the fulfillment of Children's identity rights and important documents lost due to emergency situations as referred to in paragraph (1) letter n shall be carried out by the Regency Government.

