b. educators;
c. education personnel;
d. families; and/ ore. the Community, in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.

Article 76

1. Special Protection for Child Victims of Physical and/or Psychological Violence as referred to in Article 32 paragraph (1) letter i shall be carried out through efforts to:a. disseminate and socialize the provisions of laws and regulations that protect child victims of violence; andb. monitor, report, and impose sanctions.
2. Special Protection as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be provided in the form of:a. prevention;
b. assistance;
c. medical rehabilitation; andd. Social Rehabilitation.
3. Handling of Child Victims of Physical and/or Psychological Violence as referred to in paragraph (2) shall be implemented in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.

